{"units": [{"id": "haima-quote37", "translation": "Do not cast a drop of blood upon the ground."}, {"id": "haima-quote38", "translation": "with sprinklings of blood from a slain pig"}, {"id": "haima-quote39", "translation": "with kindred streams of blood"}, {"id": "haima-quote40", "translation": "of blood that flowed from a good death"}, {"id": "haima-quote41", "translation": "through blood drunk up by the nurturing earth"}, {"id": "haima-quote42", "translation": "from the blood of his father"}, {"id": "haima-quote43", "translation": "wretched Orestes brought to a head the blood of many"}, {"id": "haima-quote44", "translation": "lifting the grim pollution of blood"}, {"id": "haima-quote45", "translation": "the smell of mortal blood"}, {"id": "haima-quote46", "translation": "the wretched blood of citizens"}, {"id": "haima-quote47", "translation": "you undertook to receive fresh blood"}, {"id": "haima-quote48", "translation": "though he is strong, nevertheless we weaken him, young blood"}, {"id": "haima-quote49", "translation": "judge this blood"}, {"id": "haima-quote50", "translation": "he has escaped the penalty for blood"}, {"id": "haima-quote51", "translation": "no banishment for blood, once they are recognized"}, {"id": "haima-quote52", "translation": "so that kindred blood will not be shed"}, {"id": "haima-quote53", "translation": "of older blood"}, {"id": "haima-quote54", "translation": "the earth, stained by the pollutions of ancient blood, sent them up"}, {"id": "haima-quote55", "translation": "for we are born from your blood"}, {"id": "haima-quote56", "translation": "blood of a full brother and of a common father"}, {"id": "haima-quote57", "translation": "in the blood of my mother"}, {"id": "haima-quote58", "translation": "does he pray away the dearest blood of his mother?"}, {"id": "haima-quote59", "translation": "and not yet is the blood of the gods faded for them"}, {"id": "haima-word1", "translation": "by fresh blood"}, {"id": "haima-word2", "translation": "of the house"}, {"id": "haimassō-orth1", "translation": "to stain with blood"}, {"id": "haimassō-def1", "translation": "to stain with blood"}, {"id": "haimassō-quote1", "translation": "staining the hearths of the gods with sheep"}, {"id": "haimassō-quote2", "translation": "and the island stained with blood on its soil"}, {"id": "haimassō-quote3", "translation": "to stain the paternal ground with blood"}, {"id": "haimassō-quote4", "translation": "to stain the ground with blood for the sake of women"}, {"id": "haimatēros-orth1", "translation": "bloody"}, {"id": "haimatēros-def1", "translation": "bloody"}, {"id": "haimatēros-quote1", "translation": "a bloody vessel"}, {"id": "haimatēros-quote2", "translation": "bloody might"}, {"id": "haimatēros-quote3", "translation": "the bloody crash of rain that destroys the house"}, {"id": "haimatēros-quote4", "translation": "bloody strife"}, {"id": "haimatēros-quote5", "translation": "bloody breath"}, {"id": "haimatēros-quote6", "translation": "bloody deeds"}, {"id": "haimatēros-quote7", "translation": "bloody whetstones"}, {"id": "haimatēphoros-orth1", "translation": "blood-bearing"}, {"id": "haimatēphoros-def1", "translation": "blood-bearing"}, {"id": "haimatēphoros-quote1", "translation": "blood-bearing deaths"}, {"id": "haimatizō-orth1", "translation": "to stain with blood"}, {"id": "haimatizō-def1", "translation": "to stain with blood"}, {"id": "haimatizō-quote1", "translation": "to stain the ground of the earth with corpses"}, {"id": "haimatoeis-orth1", "translation": "bloody"}, {"id": "haimatoeis-def1", "translation": "bloody"}, {"id": "haimatoeis-note1", "translation": "Thus I corrected what is in M φοίνισσαμυγμοῖς [bloody gashes], which arose from the gloss φοινισσομένη [being reddened], as Hesychius explains αἷματωσαι [to make bloody] by φοινίξαι [to redden]."}, {"id": "haimatoeis-quote1", "translation": "bloody bleatings"}, {"id": "haimatoeis-quote2", "translation": "bloody root"}, {"id": "haimatoeis-quote3", "translation": "bloody strife"}, {"id": "haimatoeis-quote4", "translation": "bloody blow"}, {"id": "haimatoeis-quote5", "translation": "the cheek is conspicuous, bloodied with gashes"}, {"id": "haimatoeis-quote6", "translation": "bloody wars"}, {"id": "haimatoeis-word1", "translation": "M φοίνισσαμυγμοῖς [bloody gashes]"}, {"id": "haimatoeis-word2", "translation": "φοινισσομένη [being reddened]"}, {"id": "haimatoeis-word3", "translation": "αἷματωσαι [to make bloody]"}, {"id": "haimatoeis-word4", "translation": "φοινίξαι [to redden]"}, {"id": "haimatoloichos-orth1", "translation": "blood-licking"}, {"id": "haimatoloichos-def1", "translation": "blood-licking"}, {"id": "haimatoloichos-quote1", "translation": "blood-licking desire"}, {"id": "haimatorrophos-orth1", "translation": "blood-sucking"}, {"id": "haimatorrophos-def1", "translation": "blood-sucking"}, {"id": "haimatorrophos-quote1", "translation": "the den of a blood-sucking lion"}, {"id": "haimatostagēs-orth1", "translation": "dripping with blood"}, {"id": "haimatostagēs-def1", "translation": "dripping with blood"}, {"id": "haimatostagēs-note1", "translation": "(thus from the apograph instead of αἱματοσφαγής [slaughtered in blood])"}, {"id": "haimatostagēs-note2", "translation": "Thus Stanley instead of δειματοσταγ᾽ ἐς [dripping with terror], which is in M."}, {"id": "haimatostagēs-note3", "translation": "On Eum. 366 see under αἱματόφυρτος [defiled with blood]."}, {"id": "haimatostagēs-quote1", "translation": "corpses dripping with blood"}, {"id": "haimatostagēs-quote2", "translation": "murder — dripping with blood"}, {"id": "haimatostagēs-quote3", "translation": "a libation dripping with blood"}, {"id": "haimatostagēs-quote4", "translation": "there would be a burden dripping with blood from murder"}, {"id": "haimatostagēs-word1", "translation": "αἱματοσφαγής [slaughtered in blood]"}, {"id": "haimatostagēs-word2", "translation": "δειματοσταγ᾽ ἐς [dripping with terror]"}, {"id": "haimatostagēs-word3", "translation": "αἱματόφυρτος [defiled with blood]"}, {"id": "haimatophyrtos-orth1", "translation": "defiled with blood"}, {"id": "haimatophyrtos-def1", "translation": "defiled with blood"}, {"id": "haimatophyrtos-note1", "translation": "Thus I corrected instead of αἱματοσταγές [dripping with blood], which is contrary to the meter."}, {"id": "haimatophyrtos-quote1", "translation": "a race defiled with blood"}, {"id": "haimatophyrtos-word1", "translation": "αἱματοσταγές [dripping with blood]"}, {"id": "haimorrytos-orth1", "translation": "flowing with blood"}, {"id": "haimorrytos-def1", "translation": "flowing with blood"}, {"id": "haimorrytos-quote1", "translation": "veins flowing with blood"}, {"id": "haimos-orth1", "translation": "thicket"}, {"id": "haimos-def1", "translation": "thicket"}, {"id": "haimos-note1", "translation": "Bekker's Anecdota p. 310, 3 αἱμούς: τοὺς δρυμούς [thickets: the woods]. Perhaps from the same root from which αἱμασιά [a wall of dry stones] is also said. αἵμους [thickets] falsely, as it seems, in accent, and δρυμούς [woods] corrupted into δρόμους [courses] in Eustathius p. 1851, 27. Hesychius αἱμοί: δρυμοί [thickets: woods] (αἱμοίδρυμοι [thicket-woods] in the codex). Aeschylus in the Aetnaeae."}, {"id": "haimos-word1", "translation": "αἱμούς: τοὺς δρυμούς. ἴσως ἀπὸ τοῦ αὐτοῦ ἀφ᾽ οὗ καὶ ἡ αἱμασιά λέγεται. αἵμους [thickets: the woods. Perhaps from the same root from which αἱμασιά is also said. thickets]"}, {"id": "haimos-word2", "translation": "δρυμούς [woods]"}, {"id": "haimos-word3", "translation": "δρόμους [courses]"}, {"id": "haimos-word4", "translation": "αἱμοί: δρυμοί (αἱμοίδρυμοι [thickets: woods (thicket-woods]"}, {"id": "haimos-word5", "translation": "Αἰσχύλος Αἰτναίαις [Aeschylus in the Aetnaeae]"}, {"id": "haimylos-orth1", "translation": "wily"}, {"id": "haimylos-def1", "translation": "wily"}, {"id": "haimylos-quote1", "translation": "wily devices"}, {"id": "haimōn-orth1", "translation": "bloody"}, {"id": "haimōn-def1", "translation": "bloody"}]}